zac:51192_lot_26_title rdfs:label "LIMESTONE RELIEF.  XVIIIth.dynasty.  A figure from a procession. The body is human, the head that of an antelope, adorned with a long wig. In the right hand is the khopeche, in the left a lance. The left hand of the adjoining figure is seen, bearing an ear of corn; whence it is supposed that the bas-relief represented a feast in the honour of Osiris.  Ht.,22 inches,W.,17inches" .

zac:51192_lot_27 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "LIMESTONE RELIEF.  XVIIIth.dynasty.  The head of a negro prisoner, wearing a small round wig, suggestive of curls, and a ring in his ear ; a head remarkable for its life and character. The rope which is passed several times round the prisoner's neck is knotted, and ends in a flower.  (Illustrated.)" ;
