zac:51192_lot_337 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "ITALIAN MASTER.  The rape of the Palladium.  Diomedes is represented seated, in profile, on a cubic altar decorated with laurel ; his left leg is drawn up. In his right hand he holds a short sword, and in his left, the Palladium. Reproduction of an antique engraved gem, catalogued in the inventory of the Medici family.  Bargello.Molinier,No.31.  Flattened oval, slightly concave ; beaded edge.  Ht.,2 inches.Width,1 5/8 inches.  (Illustrated.)" ;
