zac:51192_lot_342_title rdfs:label "RICCIO. Padua:1470-1532. Allegory of the culture of trees. A standing child, nude, with a loose short cloak foating from his shoulders, treading with his left foot on a prostrate satyr. He waters a tree with a can, and with the other arm shields its topmost branches from the breath of Boreas.  A perfect specimen.  Diameter,17/8inches.  Molinier, No.244. Migeon, No.329. Bode, No.711.  (Illustrated.)" .

zac:51192_lot_343 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "FRANCESCO DA SANT' AGATA. Padua:about 1500. Important bronze plaque, in high relief; representing the entombment of Christ.  On the left, four Holy Women. The body of Christ is supported above the tomb by Joseph of Arimathea. Three bearded male figures on the right. Background of hills, trees, and the Cross.  A work of remarkable force;extremely rare. Cire perdue.  Ht.,63/4inches.Width,51/2inches.  (Illustrated.)" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:51192_lot_343_title ;
