zac:51192_lot_358_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """358 — SPERANDIO.\r
\r
Virgilio Malvezzi : a nobleman of Bologna. Ambassador in 1451. Died 1481.\r
\r
Bust in profile, facing left.\r
\r
VIRGILIUS. MALVITIUS.BONON. PATRIE.DECUS. ET.LIBERTATIS.CUSTOS.\r
\r
Reverse:MCCCCLXXVIIII.-OPUS. SPERANDEI.\r
\r
left foot on a dragon, and a sword in his hand.\r
\r
An old man, nude, with floating drapery, seated with his\r
\r
Armand,vol.I.\r
\r
Diameter,3 1/2inches.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
