zac:51192_lot_501 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "PERSIAN PRAYER RUG. 16th.century. Of very fine wool; ornamented with fowers and arabesques on red ground, and framed in a fine design, with a rich border.  This rug, in an admirable state of preservation, almost exactly forms a pair with that formerly in the possession of the Emperor of Austria,at Shonbrunn. (See Dr.F.R. Martin's \" History of Oriental Carpets\", Vol. I, p. 127, fig.331.)" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:51192_lot_501_title ;
