zac:51192_lot_63_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """63 — MARBLE HEAD.\r
\r
A very fine archaic head of Athene,in Parian marble, with traces of earth. A helmet of some other material was pro- bably set on the back of the head.\r
\r
An important work,representing the transition from archaic art to the art of the 5th.century.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
\r
Ht.,7 1/4 inches.\r
## 62-MARBLETORSOOFAMAN. EarlyVth.century B.C.\r
\r
Carrying a wine-skin over the left shoulder.\r
\r
Ht.,22 1/2inches.\r
\r
About 500 B.C.\r
\r
From thePozzi collection.""",
        """63—MARBLE HEAD.\r
\r
A very fine archaic head of Athene, in Parian marble,with traces of earth.A helmet of some other material was probably set on the back of the head.\r
\r
An important work,representing the transition from archaic art to the art of the 5th.century.\r
\r
Ht.,7 1/4 inches.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
\r
