zac:51192_lot_67 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "WHITE MARBLE HEAD. IVth. to IIIrd century B.C. A very beautiful head of a woman. Part of the crown of the head is missing, but the face is intact. The hair is drawn back to a knot at the back; the head is turned slightly aside, and the eyes cast downward with a sweet and melancholy expression. The mouth and chin, particularly as seen in profile, are modelled with much delicacy. Evidently the work of a great artist.  Part of nose restored in plaster." ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:51192_lot_67_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:51192_lot_67_id ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://w3id.org/zac/type/marmi> ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:51192_lot_67_description .

