zac:5739_lot_13 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "FLEMISH MASTER OF THE DEATH OF THE VIRGIN  Flourished in the first half of the XVI century at Museum.The artist has been identifed with Josef  Gologne,the picture of that name being in the Cologne Cleef or Cleve the Elder (Joos van der Beke) circa 1490-1540. MADONNA AND CHILD SAAC KOEDYCK. The Virgin is clad in blue and draped in a scarlet cloak, holding the Child, in a loose robe of light blue; the Infant is seated on a mossgreen velvet cloth spread over a stone table. A faience pot at the left holds flowers, of which the Child has plucked one with the right hand. An embrasure at the upper right in the paneled wall behind offers a view over wooded landscape beyond.  On wood:Height,174 inches;width,121/2 inches." ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5739_lot_13_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5739_lot_13_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5739_lot_13_description .

