    rdfs:label "FERDINAND BOL  Dutch;born at Dordrecht 16il, died in Amsterdam 168o. Pupil of Rembrandt, whose studio he entered about 1630. MAN WITH A BLACK SKULL-CAP,HOLDING A BOOK. Half-length figure seated in an armchair, facing the observer; clad in sober black, with a white ruff and black skull-cap covering a head fringed with white hair. In the left hand a booka Latin treatise on botany-in the right, horn spectacles. The face is of great dignity, with blue eyes, full straight nose, white moustache and straggling beard. At the right is the inscription: \"Aetatis 66 ANo1641.\"  On Panel:Height,3217/ inches; width,25 inches." ;
