zac:5739_lot_24 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "JOACHIM PATINIR  Born about 1485 at Dinant. Settled at Antwerp in 1515.Died October 5,1524. (A) LANDSGAPE WITH A CONVENT Concluded. The hollow mountain with the fortresslike monastery, at the entrance of the semicircular huge cavity, is also seen in Patinir's more detailed picture representing the Rest on the Flight to Egypt, property of the Museum at Berlin. Right above the convent, the glorification of a saint (St. Mary of Egypt?), caught up to Heaven, is faintly visible.  Oak Panel:Height,104 inches;length,14 inches.  Note: The little owl,visible just above the saint, is by no means to be interpreted as the \"signature\" of Henri met de Bles, called 'Civetta,whose technique and colorings are very different. (B) LANDSCAPE WITH ST.JEROME AS HERMIT  A view of rocks, seashore, a town on a bay, etc. The scenery is aniwhole is whimsical but pleasing; the workmanship refined to a high degree. Patinir repeated the same motive of curious rock formation and background in a large landscape under a quite similar sky, now in the Prado Gallery at Madrid.  Oak Panel:Height,10 inches; length,13 inches." ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5739_lot_24_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5739_lot_24_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5739_lot_24_description ;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by zac:creation_5739_lot_24 .

zac:5739_lot_24_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """## 24-(A) LANDSGAPE WITH A CONVENT\r
\r
The hollow mountain with the fortresslike monastery, at the entrance of the semicircular huge cavity, is also seen in Patinir's more detailed picture representing the Rest on the Flight to Egypt, property of the Museum at Berlin. Right above the convent, the glorification of a saint (St. Mary of Egypt?), caught up to Heaven, is faintly visible.\r
\r
Oak Panel:Height,104 inches;length,14 inches.\r
\r
Note: The little owl,visible just above the saint, is by no means to be interpreted as the "signature" of Henri met de Bles, called 'Civetta,whose technique and colorings are very different.\r
\r
[Continued\r
## JOACHIM PATINIR\r
\r
Born about 1485 at Dinant. Settled at Antwerp in 1515. Died October 5,1524. 24-Concluded\r
\r
(B) LANDSCAPE WITH ST.JEROME AS HERMIT\r
\r
A view of rocks, seashore, a town on a bay, etc. The scenery is aniwhole is whimsical but pleasing; the workmanship refined to a high degree. Patinir repeated the same motive of curious rock formation and background in a large landscape under a quite similar sky, now in the Prado Gallery at Madrid.\r
\r
Oak Panel:Height,10 inches; length,13 inches.\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

