    rdfs:label "BARTHOLOMEW BRUYN THE ELDER  ## (Attributed to)  Born 1493 at Wesel. Settled at Cologne. Died there. PORTRAITS OF A DONOR AND HIS WIFE IN THE ACT OF ADORATION The wings of a triptych; landscape backgrounds. The man, wearing a long, fair beard, is dressed in an ample black robe and a cap of the same color. The woman is wearing a white headdress and black raiment with white lining and a broad belt of gold leather.  On wood:Height, 26 inches; width,9/4 inches.  Formerly in the Collection J.E. Taylor. The central panel accord- ing to reliable information in the de Merode Gallery at Brussels." ;
