zac:5739_lot_34 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "“THE MASTER OF MOULINS\" Identical with the\"Painter of the Bourbons:\"French school, second half of the XV Century. Active still about 1500. LIFE SIZE,HALF-LENGTH FIGURE OF A LADY IN THE ATTITUDE OF PRAYER  She is represented in a garden, bounded by a brick-wall, and wears a brown dress, set off with dark brown fur. The cherry-red sleeves of her undergarment are just visible at the wrists. Same color in her headdress, bordered with faint gold, and a necklace of gold. Important fragment of the right wing of a very large triptych, as is proved by the reverse side showing the vertical broad drapery of a standing figure, undoubtedly a saint. A masterpiece of most sincere expression.  Oak Panel:Height,214 inches; width,1834 inches.  （In the right upper corner, behind the head of the woman, a piece of wood is set in.)" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5739_lot_34_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5739_lot_34_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5739_lot_34_description ;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by zac:creation_5739_lot_34 .

zac:5739_lot_34_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """## 34-LIFE SIZE,HALF-LENGTH FIGURE OF A LADY IN\r
\r
## THE ATTITUDE OF PRAYER\r
\r
She is represented in a garden, bounded by a brick-wall, and wears a brown dress, set off with dark brown fur. The cherry-red sleeves of her undergarment are just visible at the wrists. Same color in her headdress, bordered with faint gold, and a necklace of gold. Important fragment of the right wing of a very large triptych, as is proved by the reverse side showing the vertical broad drapery of a standing figure, undoubtedly a saint. A masterpiece of most sincere expression.\r
\r
Oak Panel:Height,214 inches; width,1834 inches.\r
\r
（In the right upper corner, behind the head of the woman, a piece of wood is set in.)\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

