zac:5739_lot_39 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "HANS MEMLING  Born about 1430. Pupil of Rogier van der Weyden.  Settled at Bruges. Died August 11, 1494. THE PENANCE OF ST.JEROME IN A LANDSGAPE. The right wing of a rather large triptych, reduced to become complete in itself. The Saint is dressed in a ragged coat of a violetbrown color. Behind him in the foreground iris and other fowers are growing. In the background two hermits praying near a spring, and （on the left,half missing)t the group of St. George liberating the princess by killing the dragon. Landscape and figures are excellent in workmanship and perspective. The picture is extraordinarily expressive.  Oak Panel:Height,1814 inches;width,13% inches.  Formerly in the Collection of Vicomte Bernard d'Hendecourt,  London." ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5739_lot_39_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5739_lot_39_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5739_lot_39_description ;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by zac:creation_5739_lot_39 .

