zac:5739_lot_47 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "GIOVANNI BATTISTA TIEPOLO  Born in Venice 1696. Died 177o. Piaxzetta and Paolo Veronese were his teachers; but he has, by his great genius, elevated the Venetian style of painting of the \"Settecento\" to a height which excelled even that of the French painting of the same period. A BISHOP READING THE PRAYER. The background is niche-fashioned, and in the extrados two figures in grisaille are lying along the curve of the arch. In the niche a bishop, assisted by an acolyte, reads the prayer from a book which a page, kneeling, holds up to him. A sketch for some unknown picture. Tiepolo is particularly happy in his sketches, which show more the freshness of his imagination than the great compositions for which they are intended. The composition, forms and color all unite in pointing to Tiepolo as the author.  Height,23%4 inches;width,1334 inches" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5739_lot_47_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5739_lot_47_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5739_lot_47_description ;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by zac:creation_5739_lot_47 .

