zac:5739_lot_48 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "VINCENZO CATENA  Venetian painter; worked under Giovanni Bellini. Died 1531. PORTRAIT OF A MAN WITH A BEARD. Bust-size, three-quarter turned to right, with cap and dress of brownish-crimson on a dark background. The cold and fat treatment of the face, the breadth of the shoulders and other peculiarities point quite distinctly to Catena as the author. The picture was, long ago, enlarged by about one inch to the right, in order to make it fit the  Height,18 inches; width, 15 inches.  old frame.  From the Fairfax Murray Collection." ;
