zac:5739_lot_53 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "LORENZO VENEZIANO  (Worked at Venice between 1357 and 1359). ST.NICHOLAS BOUNTY n a room, standing in an attitude of humility,before their father, are the three maidens whom St. Nicholas saves from dishonor by throwing to them, from a window, the three golden balls which are to be their dowry. It is a pendant to No.52, and like it, is beautiful and perfectly preserved." ;
