zac:5739_lot_54_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """## 54-MADONNA AND CHILD\r
\r
On a gold background is the half-length figure of the Madonna, turned three-quarters to the right, holding the Child. The face and hands of the Virgin distinctly point to Segna as the author. It was evidently the centre panel of a polyptych.\r
\r
Height, 34 inches; width, 23%4 inches.\r
\r
Formerly of S. Miniato dei Tedeschi, near Florence.\r
\r
Note: See, Duccio and his School by G. De Nicola in the "Burlington Magazine, Dec. 1912,P.I46.\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

zac:5739_lot_54_id a crm:E42_Identifier ;
    rdfs:label "BO0624_5739-54" .

zac:5739_lot_54_title rdfs:label "SEGNA DI BONAVENTURA  Worked between the end of the XII and the beginning of the XIII Gentury. With Ugolino, he was the most faithful disciple of Duccio,the founder of the Sienese school of painting. MADONNA AND CHILD. On a gold background is the half-length figure of the Madonna, turned three-quarters to the right, holding the Child. The face and hands of the Virgin distinctly point to Segna as the author. It was evidently the centre panel of a polyptych.  Height, 34 inches; width, 23%4 inches.  Formerly of S. Miniato dei Tedeschi, near Florence.  Note: See, Duccio and his School by G. De Nicola in the \"Burlington Magazine, Dec. 1912,P.I46." .

zac:5739_lot_55 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "GIOVANNI ANTONIO BOLTRAFFIO  Born in Milan 1467. Died 1516.The most gifted of Leonardi da Vinci's pupils:a Madonna at Budapest and the \"Casio\" panel at the Louure are among his works. THE VIRGIN WITH THE BOOK. The half-length figure of the Madonna is shown behind the parapet on the ledge of which the Child is seated. Her right hand rests From two openings in the rear is seen the landscape of the background. The pretty and novel idea of this composition pleased the Master so much that he reproduced it in a picture which was in on a book, and with her left she is offering a flower to the Child. the Loeser Collection at Florence.  Height,21 inches; width,15% inches.  From the Crespi Collection at Milano, and before that it was in the Colbacchini Collection at Venice.  Note: See,A.Venturi, The Crespi Gallery (Milan, Hoepli 1goo), p. 237.  See, G. Carotti, G. A. Boltraffio in the National Italian Gallery (Rome, 1899), vol. IV,Pp.305and329.  See, B. Berenson, North Italian Painters of the Renaissance.  Mentioned in the catalogue of the Musee de Breca de Milan, Pp. 181-182; also in Baedeker and in the Guide Joanne." ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5739_lot_55_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5739_lot_55_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5739_lot_55_description ;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by zac:creation_5739_lot_55 .

