    rdfs:label """## 55-THE VIRGIN WITH THE BOOK\r
\r
The half-length figure of the Madonna is shown behind the parapet on the ledge of which the Child is seated. Her right hand rests From two openings in the rear is seen the landscape of the background. The pretty and novel idea of this composition pleased the Master so much that he reproduced it in a picture which was in on a book, and with her left she is offering a flower to the Child. the Loeser Collection at Florence.\r
\r
Height,21 inches; width,15% inches.\r
\r
From the Crespi Collection at Milano, and before that it was in the Colbacchini Collection at Venice.\r
\r
Note: See,A.Venturi, The Crespi Gallery (Milan, Hoepli 1goo), p. 237.\r
\r
See, G. Carotti, G. A. Boltraffio in the National Italian Gallery (Rome, 1899), vol. IV,Pp.305and329.\r
\r
See, B. Berenson, North Italian Painters of the Renaissance.\r
\r
Mentioned in the catalogue of the Musee de Breca de Milan, Pp. 181-182; also in Baedeker and in the Guide Joanne.\r
##""" ;
