zac:5739_lot_56 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "VITTORE BELLINIANO  A Venetian painter of the first decade of the XVI Gentury. He was, for a time, assistant to Giambellino. PORTRAITS OF TWO YOUNG VENETIAN NOBLES. Busts, turned slightly towards each other, dark background. The the Kaiser Friedrich Museum of Berlin where it was on view until 1922 (see, H. Posse, Die Gemalde Galerie des Kaiser-Friedrich Museum I, 1913, p. 127. n. 12), in which year it was allowed to go in order to make place for a Durer. Because of the steadiness of the drawing and a certain grandiosity in the style of reproducing the characteristics of his subject, one were inclined rather to assign the work to Cariani. In the Louvre there is a replica of this, but not so powerful and of a later period.  Height,1734 inches;length,241 inches.  From the Solly Collection in London." ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5739_lot_56_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5739_lot_56_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5739_lot_56_description ;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by zac:creation_5739_lot_56 .

