    rdfs:label "PARIS BORDONE  Born at Treviso 1500. Died at Venice 1571. AUTUMN. On the right the figure of a woman, suggesting Diana, to whom a satyr offers grapes. Cupid is coming toward her with roses which are being picked by Flora, on the left. This allegory has a pendant  Height,421/ inches;length,63 inches.  in the Vienna Gallery.  Note: Belonged to the Paul Delaroff Collection of St. Petersburg, afterwards to the Sedelmeyer Collection at Paris. It is reproduced under No. 31, in the 1gi3 Catalogue of Paintings by Old Masters, of the Sedelmeyer Collection." ;
