zac:5739_lot_6_title rdfs:label "ROELANDT SAVERY  Born at Courtrai 1576. Died in Utrecht 1639. A ROCKY WOODLAND LANDSGAPE On the right a group of lions before trees; various remains of ani mals devoured by them in the foreground. On the left,near a high cascade, several panthers, and in the sky a large bird of prey.  On wood:Height,151/ inches;length,2814 inches." .

zac:5739_lot_7 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "GUILLIAM (WILLEM) VAN HERP  Born at Antwerp about 16i4.Pupil of Damiaan Wortelmans,and later,in 1628,of Biermans.Died at Antwerp 1677. THE FOUR SEASONS THE FOUR SEASONS (Concluded) (A) SpRING; symbolized by shearing sheep, done by an old man, assisted by a boy. On the right two women are preparing dinner; one gives a bowl to a boy, and a young man, with a stick over his shoulder to which are attached two cocks, is looking at the scene.  On wood:Height,1734 inches;length,25%4 inches.  - (B) SuMMER; symbolized by a huntsman with three dogs on the left, and a group of four peasants, two men and two women on the right. One of the women is milking a goat.  On wood:Height,17/ inches; length,25/ inches. （C) AuTuMN; symbolized by the vintage. On the right various persons collecting grapes accompanied by a dog; in the centre a man with bare feet treading grapes; on the left a man putting grapes into a tub and a woman on her knees testing the mash. - (D) WINTER; a snowy landscape symbolizing winter. In the centre of the landscape two men are loading fire-wood on an ass, a third one, on the left is chopping wood, near him a dog. On the right two ducks are swimming and in the background is a house, with people before it preparing the meal.  On wood:Height,1734 inches;length,2512 inches.  On wood:Height,17/ inches;length,25 inches," ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5739_lot_7_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5739_lot_7_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5739_lot_7_description ;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by zac:creation_5739_lot_7 .

