zac:5750_lot_13 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "LORENZO DA SAN SEVERINO  AB0UT 1374-—1420  With his brother Jacopo of the Salimbeni, Lorenzo was the principal exponent of art in the Marche for a generation preceding Gentile da Fabriano. TRIPTYCH:VIRGIN AND CHILD. In the central panel is depicted the Virgin Mother enthroned with the Infant Christ; an angel kneels at her feet offering gifts. In the left panel a saintly mitred Bishop stands, slightly turned towards the Virgin. In the right panel Saint Christopher is represented bearing the Child Christ upon his shoulder and crossing the turbid stream." ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5750_lot_13_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5750_lot_13_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5750_lot_13_description ;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by zac:creation_5750_lot_13 .

zac:5750_lot_13_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """In the central panel is depicted the Virgin Mother enthroned with the Infant Christ; an angel kneels at her feet offering gifts. In the left panel a saintly mitred Bishop stands, slightly turned towards the Virgin. In the right panel Saint Christopher is represented bearing the Child Christ upon his shoulder and crossing the turbid stream.\r
\r
Height,29 inches;length,461 inches.\r
\r
Note: The principal reference work for the art of Lorenzo is his signed triptych in the Gallery of San Severino, compared with which this picture of the Chiesa Collection presents the same decorative style (which fundamentally characterizes the so-called international art of the beginning of the fifteenth century) although in a rather less accentuated form. One cannot say definitely whether this is the result of a diminished enthusiasm on the part of the master himself during a certain period, or the effect of his collaboration to a marked degree with his brother Jacopo.\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

zac:5750_lot_13_id a crm:E42_Identifier ;
    rdfs:label "BO0624_5750-13" .

zac:5750_lot_13_title rdfs:label "LORENZO DA SAN SEVERINO  AB0UT 1374-—1420  With his brother Jacopo of the Salimbeni, Lorenzo was the principal exponent of art in the Marche for a generation preceding Gentile da Fabriano. TRIPTYCH:VIRGIN AND CHILD. In the central panel is depicted the Virgin Mother enthroned with the Infant Christ; an angel kneels at her feet offering gifts. In the left panel a saintly mitred Bishop stands, slightly turned towards the Virgin. In the right panel Saint Christopher is represented bearing the Child Christ upon his shoulder and crossing the turbid stream." .

