zac:5750_lot_2_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """## 2.A HOLY BISHOP (SAINT AUGUSTINE?)\r
\r
Seated,in an attitude of benediction,between Saint Mark and Saint Anthony; the three figures seen at half-length.\r
\r
\r
\r
This is a very fine example of the master's work, being of his advanced period, and revealing the ecstatic emotions produced by\r
the paintings of Giambellino supplemented by an animation inspired by Lorenzo Lotto. The picture is in a good state of preservation.\r
\r
Canvas:Height,13/ inches;length,15 inches.\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

zac:5750_lot_2_id a crm:E42_Identifier ;
    rdfs:label "BO0624_5750-2" .

zac:5750_lot_2_title rdfs:label "ANDREA PREVITALI  Worked between 1502 and 1525, first emulating the style of Giovanni Bellini, and afterwards that of Lotto. A HOLY BISHOP (SAINT AUGUSTINE?). Seated,in an attitude of benediction,between Saint Mark and Saint Anthony; the three figures seen at half-length.    This is a very fine example of the master's work, being of his advanced period, and revealing the ecstatic emotions produced by the paintings of Giambellino supplemented by an animation inspired by Lorenzo Lotto. The picture is in a good state of preservation." .

