zac:5750_lot_32 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "SCHOOL OF AVIGNON. XV CENTURY. THE MOURNING FOR CHRIST" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5750_lot_32_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5750_lot_32_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5750_lot_32_description .

zac:5750_lot_32_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """## 32.THE MOURNING FOR CHRIST\r
\r
An intensive and interesting composition in which the figure of the Mother, the two Marys, St. John to the left, and the aged\r
\r
Saviour lies emaciated and inert upon a marble sarcophagus. Behind are grouped, with great forethought and reverence, the holy Joseph of Arimathea; to the right, in the background, is the head of Nicodemus, or maybe that of the donor; on the extreme left a distant vista of the hill of Golgotha. The Madonna as the central and predominant figure of the composition is robed in a blue-black mantle, and wears an opaque-white hood that detracts from the fesh of our Lord, which in comparison appears limpid and ashy; Saint John in a cloak of vivid and beautiful red; Joseph of Arimathea wears an ample garb of brocade and fur. A very important and rare work.\r
\r
Oak panel (rounded at the two upper corners):Height,19 inches; length, 271/2inches.\r
\r
The Collection of Rudolph Kahn.\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

zac:5750_lot_32_id a crm:E42_Identifier ;
    rdfs:label "BO0624_5750-32" .

zac:5750_lot_32_title rdfs:label "SCHOOL OF AVIGNON. XV CENTURY. THE MOURNING FOR CHRIST" .

zac:5750_lot_33 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "MASOLINO DA PANICALE  (ATTRIBUTED TO) 1383-1440- MADONNA AND CHILD" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5750_lot_33_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5750_lot_33_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5750_lot_33_description ;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by zac:creation_5750_lot_33 .

zac:5750_lot_33_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """## 33.MADONNA AND CHILD\r
\r
The holy Mother is shown at half-length, facing slightly to the right, with an expression of great beauty, wearing a gracefully draped hood and mantle; in her arms is the Child Christ fully draped in a crimson robe, girdled at the waist and holding a bird. His expression of supreme joy naively portrayed. The nimbi are exquisitely wrought in bulino work.\r
\r
Panel:Height,27 inches;width,23 inches.\r
\r
Note: This work, by a master of the first half of the xV Century, possesses much of the modeling of the Madonna and the formation of her right hand. Compare the Madonna in the Bremen Museum.\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

zac:5750_lot_33_id a crm:E42_Identifier ;
