zac:5750_lot_4 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "MICHELE MARIESCHI  VENETIAN:1696—1743. LANDSCAPE. Fantastic view. To the right is a ruined Romanesque-Renaissance structure having fine Corinthian pillars and capitals, which are overgrown with ivy; in the middle distance, the river fowing under a somewhat dilapidated bridge; on the near bank are various small figures of armored warriors; on the far bank, undulating landscape; a partly ruined arc, and on the summit of the hill a fortified chateau. An imaginative work portrayed in brilliant colors.  Height,29 inches;width,38 inches." ;
