zac:5750_lot_43 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "MICHELANGELO BUONARROTI  (ATTRIBUTED TO) 1475-1564. THE CRESPI MADONNA" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5750_lot_43_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5750_lot_43_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5750_lot_43_description ;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by zac:creation_5750_lot_43 .

zac:5750_lot_43_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """43. THE CRESPI MADONNA\r
\r
Halflength fgure of the Virgin, seen in profle, the head turned to the left.She holds in her arms the Child,Who,laughing,is turned a little to the right, and clings to her neck with His left hand; with His right He clasps the right hand of His Mother. The background consists of a mountainous landscape.The grandeur, be it of the group as a whole, or of each separate figure, is truly Michelangelesque, and the types are absolutely his. Some participation on the part of the master is beyond doubt, at least in the sketch of the painting. All the easel works, except the tondo of the Holy Family in the Uffizi, which are attributed to Michelangelo, are disputable. In this Crespi Madonna are seen the same probabilities as in the example in the London National Gallery and that at Dublin, and therefore, equally, they should be attributed with the same hesitation.\r
\r
Panel:Height,33 inches;width,24 inches.\r
\r
A proof that the painting cannot be exclusively the work of pupils lies in the fact that there is apparent in the profle, the drapery, the attitude and other details of the Madonna, a clear derivation of the Pazzi Madonna of Donatello, which is in the Kaiser Friedrich Museum at Berlin. Michelangelo, as a young man, came under the influence of Donatello, whereas an imitator of Michelangelo would, by this time, have been free from the possibility of such influence.\r
\r
See:F.Knapp,"Michelangelo (Des Meisterwerke),"Leipzig, 1907,page 148; Joanne's Guide;Baedeker, Milano;Frizzoni, "Les Arts,"1904, No. 29, p. 31-32; "Collection des Classiques de lArt Michelange’ Paris, 1909.\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

