zac:5750_lot_47_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """47.SALOME\r
\r
On the left, the executioner is in the act of placing the head of St. John the Baptist on the charger, which he offers to Salome. Behind is Herod's wife. In the background the king's banquet is glimpsed through an opening.\r
\r
ing the lute,at one time in the Hertz Collection and now in the Palazzo Venezia at Rome, and other portraits by Andrea Solario. In an excellent state of preservation.\r
\r
The picture can be compared with the portrait of a woman play-\r
\r
Panel:Height,25 inches; length,30 inches.\r
\r
The Fairfax Murray Collection.\r
\r
## ANDREA SOLARIO\r
\r
CIRCA 1460-—1530\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

