zac:5750_lot_48_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """48. TRIPTYCH:MADONNA,CHILD AND SAINTS\r
\r
The central panel depicts the half-length figure of the Madonna hooded and robed in a superb fluctuating blue mantle with a goldembroidered star at her right shoulder; the Child,half draped with a crimson cloth, is nestling against His Mother. The left panel depicts St. Paul richly robed in a green tunic and aubergine mantle, bearing a sheathed sword; the right panel, St. Peter in a tunic of a more brilliant green, and an old-gold mantle, with the keys and papal ring. In the arches above are the Redeemer, St. Mary Magdalene and St. Michael. The background is of gold. In the original tabernacolo.\r
\r
Height,5134 inches; width,50 inches.\r
\r
Gatalogued by the Italian Government, May 27,1922.\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

