zac:5750_lot_4_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """## 4.LANDSGAPE\r
\r
Fantastic view. To the right is a ruined Romanesque-Renaissance structure having fine Corinthian pillars and capitals, which are overgrown with ivy; in the middle distance, the river fowing under a somewhat dilapidated bridge; on the near bank are various small figures of armored warriors; on the far bank, undulating landscape; a partly ruined arc, and on the summit of the hill a fortified chateau. An imaginative work portrayed in brilliant colors.\r
\r
Height,29 inches;width,38 inches.\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

