zac:5750_lot_50 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "ANTONELLO DA MESSINA 1430(7)-—1479. ENERGETIC PORTRAIT OF A SICILIAN" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5750_lot_50_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5750_lot_50_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5750_lot_50_description ;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by zac:creation_5750_lot_50 .

zac:5750_lot_50_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """## 50. ENERGETIC PORTRAIT OF A SICILIAN\r
\r
## PATRICIAN IN ECCLESIASTIGAL COSTUME\r
\r
A bust portrait, holding the votive model of a church, half of which is seen at lower left of the picture.\r
\r
Senator Adolfo Venturi in 192o expressed himself critically in an article devoted to this painting and published in the bi-annual periodical Arte of 1921March to June, and republished in 1923, as follows: "A sudden brilliance, as in the Virgin with a Book at Palermo, lights the face of the Sicilian, who holds in his unseen hand the votive model of a church; the breast-wall cuts the figure at bust length, according to the usual composition of the portraits of Antonello; the head, not painted with the easy foreshortening of the Condottiero of the Louvre or of the Old Man of the Casa Trivulzio, retains the cylindrical form found in the portraits in London and Berlin, but the forceful and almost violent partition of the light and shade, a new and potent means of plastic definition, marks a similarity with the portrait of the Condottiero and affords the certainty that the work is of his first Venetian period, that is to say of the years in which the Messina family undertook at Venice the lost pala of San Cassiano."\r
\r
Note: The picture is illustrated in Arte, Adolfo Venturi,“Per Antonello da Messina”\r
\r
Panel:Height, 16 inches; width,13 inches.\r
\r
Rome,1921,and also in Arte,Rome,1923.\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

