zac:5750_lot_51_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """## 51. PORTRAIT OF THE POET MELDOLLA\r
\r
Erect figure in an architectural setting, robed in the green-black tocco of his calling with a fur stole, and resting his arm against the plinth of the two marble columns;in his right hand he holds a laurel wreath. To the left is seen an attendant female figure draped in crimson and gold supporting an amphora upon her head.\r
\r
Note: The Italian Government catalogued this work as of great national interest. The pigment has been transferred from panel to canvas.\r
\r
Panel:Height,53 inches;width,45 inches.\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

