zac:5750_lot_52 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "AGNOLO GADDI  FLORENTINE:1335(?)—1396. PAINTING ON PANEL: MADONNA AND CHILD" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5750_lot_52_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5750_lot_52_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5750_lot_52_description ;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by zac:creation_5750_lot_52 .

zac:5750_lot_52_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """52.PAINTING ON PANEL: MADONNA AND CHILD\r
\r
Upon a gold background is superimposed a draped canopy of a deep sealing-wax red, the minute design in gold bulino work, as a setting to the magnificent life-size rendering of the Madonna and Child. The blessed Virgin is seated, hooded and robed in a fucruating blue, her embroidered mantle lined with green; the Child on her arm clothed in a mauve robe, and in the hieratic attitude of benediction, with a bird perched upon His left hand. At her feet is an adoring choir of angels composed of robed cherubim and seraphim, the tones of which reveal a masterly composition of color. The canopy is also supported by angels draped in gold, their profiles of classic contour. Above are two voluminously robed angels supporting the crown as a symbol of sovereignty. Each figure is crowned by an aureole.(Tabernacolo restored.)\r
\r
Height,7 feet 2 inches;width,3 feet 9 inches.\r
\r
Catalogued by the Italian Government as a work of national impor- tance January 17,1918.\r
\r
Formerly in the Villa of Cau. Masi a Gapannoli (Toscana).\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

zac:5750_lot_52_id a crm:E42_Identifier ;
    rdfs:label "BO0624_5750-52" .

zac:5750_lot_52_title rdfs:label "AGNOLO GADDI  FLORENTINE:1335(?)—1396. PAINTING ON PANEL: MADONNA AND CHILD" .

zac:5750_lot_53 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "BERNARDO DADDI. FLORENTINE:FIRST HALF OF XIV CENTURY. PALA RUCELLAI In five segmental panels: The central panel depicts the Madonna and Child; the Blessed Virgin, hooded and robed in a green gold tunic, with an indigo-blue mantle, in her arms the fully robed Child in an attitude of infinite tenderness. The side panels from left to right depict, St. Francis of Assisi with tonsured head, robed in the olivegreen habit, and bearing a crimson bound missal; St. John in purplecrimson, the Archangel Michael in aubergine tunic, and a green cope fastened by a clasp, and carrying the unsheathed sword; St. Bernard in the black habit with hood, and an open missal. In the cusped arches are the four evangelists, and above six winged seraphim heads. The seraphim heads are a later addition of the fifteenth century;probably to give the effect of a square top and can be easily removed. Gold background." ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5750_lot_53_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5750_lot_53_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5750_lot_53_description ;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by zac:creation_5750_lot_53 .

zac:5750_lot_53_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """## 53.PALA RUCELLAI In five segmental panels: The central panel depicts the Madonna and Child; the Blessed Virgin, hooded and robed in a green gold tunic, with an indigo-blue mantle, in her arms the fully robed Child in an attitude of infinite tenderness. The side panels from left to right depict, St. Francis of Assisi with tonsured head, robed in the olivegreen habit, and bearing a crimson bound missal; St. John in purplecrimson, the Archangel Michael in aubergine tunic, and a green cope fastened by a clasp, and carrying the unsheathed sword; St. Bernard in the black habit with hood, and an open missal. In the cusped arches are the four evangelists, and above six winged seraphim heads. The seraphim heads are a later addition of the fifteenth century;probably to give the effect of a square top and can be easily removed. Gold background.\r
\r
Height,4 feet I inch;length,8 feet 5 inches.\r
\r
Note: The pala is from the Capella Rucellai in the church of San Pancrazio a Firenze, and in Italy is known as the "Pala Rucellai" Classified by the Italian Government April 6, 1918.\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

