zac:5750_lot_54_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """## 54.LARGE PALA REPRESENTING THE LEGEND OF ST.JOHN THE BAPTIST\r
\r
In the central panel is an outstanding erect full-face figure of John the Baptist,holding in his right hand a scroll inscribed:Ego vox clamantis in deserto, and in his left hand a cross. At his feet lies Herod, who, turning towards the saint, proclaims his virtues: Nos insensati vitam illorum extimabus insaniam,etc.\r
\r
base, from the top to the bottom and from left to right, are various scenes from the life of the saint in the following order:\r
\r
In the spandrels are seraphim and in the side panels and the\r
\r
- 1.THE ANNOUNCEMENT OF THE ANGEL TO ZACHARIAH. In the interior of a temple before an altar the angel is making the announcement of his impending fatherhood to Zachariah, who, in the act of prayer, is swinging a censer.\r
- IIl. THE BIRTH OF JoHN. In the bedchamber the mother, in bed, is assisted by a handmaiden, in the foreground; two other handmaidens attend the child, while a fourth is receiving gifts\r
- 1I.THE VISITATION. Mary, followed by a handmaiden, visits St. Elizabeth, who greets her, prostrating herself before her.\r
- from an old woman.\r
- hannes est nomen eius").\r
- Iv. THE CHRIsTENING. The four handmaidens in a group are presenting the babe to the priest, who names him John ("Jo-\r
- V.JoURNEY IN THE DEsERT. The young John, in sandals, with his garment of camel's hair, departs into the desert.\r
- crowd of listeners.\r
- VI. PREACHING THE GosPEL. St. John presents Christ to a\r
\r
[Continued\r
VII. THE BAPTISM OF CHRIST. On the right Christ is being baptized by St. John in the river Jordan, and two angels on the bank to the left, kneel holding an outspread cloth.\r
\r
Ix. THE MARTYRDoM OF ST. JoHN. Kneeling at the prison\r
\r
VIIl. HeRoD's FEAsT. The king and his guests at table admire Salome, who is dancing.\r
\r
- door is the saint, who is being beheaded.\r
- X.THE PRESENTATION OF THE HEAD OF THE BAPTIST. Salome, kneeling, presents to Herod the head of the saint on a charger.\r
- souls; the third in the group is the Baptist.\r
- XI. CHRIST IN LIMBO. (Base portion.) Christ, carrying the banner of victory at the threshold of Limbo, to free the\r
\r
Height (central part),42 inches;length,87 inches.\r
\r
This notable masterpiece, certainly one of the most wonderful productions of primitive Italian art, is remarkable for its originality and vigor of expression, combined with the most delicate grace of form, and in contemplating its beautiful and enamel-like finish, one does not know which to admire more-its brightness and perfect blending of colors,or its unique state of preservation.\r
\r
The Fairfax Murray Collection.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

