zac:5750_lot_55 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "FILIPPINO LIPPI  Born at Prato about 1457, the son of Filippo Lippi; died at Florence I5o4. His art developed under the guidance of his father;he also came under the infuence of Cosimo and to a great extent of Botticelli.  LEGEND OF PERSEUS" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5750_lot_55_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5750_lot_55_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5750_lot_55_description ;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by zac:creation_5750_lot_55 .

zac:5750_lot_55_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """## 55.LEGEND OF PERSEUS\r
\r
Among the many episodes in the life of the hero there are here depicted: On the left, Zeus conquers with golden rain, and Danae, who bears Perseusmother and son are placed in a boat. In the centre, King Polydictus, who cares for Danae and Perseus when they are cast by a storm on to the island of Seriphos, the same king sending Perseus, now a grown man, on his expedition against the Gorgons. On the right Perseus is seen, who, with the winged sandals of Hermes, the shield of Athena and the helm of Hades, succeeds in his quest and cuts off the head of Medusa, from whose body rises Pegasus and who is seen flying above.\r
\r
Panel:Height,2o inches;length,65 inches.\r
\r
Note: The rather accentuated movement in the figures, the generally dark tone of the coloring,would place the execution in the period of Filippino's frescoes at Santa Maria Sopra Minerva at Rome, and that agrees with the date 1492,on one of the two panels. In an excellent state of preservation; evidently the front of a coffer or espalier.\r
\r
(Gompanion to the following)\r
## FILIPPINO LIPPI\r
\r
Born at Prato about 1457, the son of Filippo Lippi; died at Florence I5o4. His art developed under the guidance of his father;he also came under the infuence of Cosimo and to a great extent of Botticelli.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

zac:5750_lot_55_id a crm:E42_Identifier ;
    rdfs:label "BO0624_5750-55" .

