    rdfs:label "WORKSHOP OF THE VIVARINI  VENICE:XV CENTURY. POLYPTYCH" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5750_lot_59_title ;
    crm:P138i_has_representation <https://historica.unibo.it/iiif-server/aa77adb9-a14e-4320-b246-94db12aff43f/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5750_lot_59_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:5750_lot_59_description .

zac:5750_lot_59_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """## 59.POLYPTYCH\r
\r
The central panel portrays the full-length figure of the girdled Madonna, within the mandorla, supported by angels; at her feet are St. Thomas and four donors in devout attitude. The side panels depict Ss.Antonio Abate,Agostino,Monica,Agostino Novello and another, unidentified.\r
\r
Central panel:Height,54 inches;width,44 inches; side panels:Height, 54 inches;width,24 inches.\r
\r
Note: The depiction of the Saints Agostiniani shows that this work was most probably executed either for a church or monastery of this Order. The work is indisputably from the workshop of the Vivarini and shows the predominant characteristics of Alvise, in the boldness of design and the sculptural realism.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

zac:5750_lot_59_id a crm:E42_Identifier ;
    rdfs:label "BO0624_5750-59" .

zac:5750_lot_59_title rdfs:label "WORKSHOP OF THE VIVARINI  VENICE:XV CENTURY. POLYPTYCH" .

zac:5750_lot_5_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """5.ST.STEPHEN AND ST. BONAVENTURA (Two Panels)\r
\r
St. Stephen stands, in the garb of a deacon,praying, with the stones of his martyrdom on his head and shoulder. The background is a rocky landscape. St. Bonaventura is also standing, turned a little to the left, reading a book which he holds in his left hand;he wears his mitre, the habit of a Franciscan under his chasuble, and carries a crosier. At his feet is a cardinal's hat. The two saints face one another: The panels are evidently parts of a triptych, the middle portion of which is missing.\r
\r
Height,58 inches; width,28 inches.\r
\r
La Galleria Conte Bassi, 7-9 November, 1898.\r
\r
See: B. Berenson,"North Italian Painters of the Renaissance” page 275;A.Venturi,La Galleria Crespi di Milano,Hoepli,90o,\r
\r
##""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

