zac:5830_lot_13_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """InscribedFrancesco Parmegiano o",and bearing the mark of the collection of Sir Joshua Reynolds.\r
## PARMEGIANO\r
\r
The Virgin, playing with the Child. A very graceful and masterly study,in sanguine.\r
\r
Ht.,7inches.W.6inches.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
## Sebastiano del PIOMBO\r
\r
Rome:1485-1547\r
\r
The Flagellation. Sepia study,for the painting in S. Pietro in Montorio, Rome.\r
\r
Ht.,16 1/2 inches.W.,12 1/2inches.\r
\r
From the Jules Dupan collection,Geneva. Stamped.)\r
\r
(Sale in Paris,1840.—\r
\r
From the collection of Count Gelozzi,Turin.(Stamped.) From the Bonaffe collection.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
## Giambattista PIRANESI\r
\r
Venice,Rome:1720-1778\r
\r
A garden, with figures, vases, and sculpture; a palace in the background.\r
\r
Sepia.\r
\r
Ht.,101/2inches.W.,14 5/8inches.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
## Nicolas POUSSIN\r
\r
Sepia drawing of the three figures on the left of the picture of  Moses striking the rock ", in the Ellesmere Collection.\r
\r
Ht.,1l inches.W.,10 1/4 inches.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

