zac:5830_lot_30_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """30\r
\r
## SPINELLO ARETINO\r
\r
Florentine School:died 1410\r
\r
St. Peter and St. Paul. Above, in a medallion, Christ. St. Paul wears a mitre and a red cloak; St. Peter, in a green dress and yellow cloak,holds a book and his key. Gold background.\r
\r
Ogival panel. Ht.,29 inches. W.,18 inches. Medallion,diameter 4inches.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
## \r
\r
\r
## \r
\r
\r
\r
## \r
## \r
## \r
##\r
\r
Florence:I5th.century\r
\r
Demarcation of the boundaries of Rome.\r
\r
A composition full of life and motion. Two oxen, an ass, mounted figures, and others, armed, on foot, in many-coloured costumes and armour; against a background of hills, trees, water, and a city.\r
\r
Panel. Ht.,19 1/4 inches.W.,26 inches. (Illustrated.)\r
## Giovanni dal PONTE\r
\r
Florence :15th.century.\r
\r
The Virgin and Child, with two angels. The Virgin's black mantle falls from her head to the ground, which is strewn with white fowers. The Child, in red,with a white mantle, caresses his Mother's face with his right hand, while with the other he clings to her breast. Gold background.\r
\r
Ogival panel.Ht.,30 1/2 inches.W.,16 1/2 inches.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
## Giovanni SANTI\r
\r
Urbino:about 1435-1494\r
\r
The Virgin and Child. The Child, nude,has fallen asleep on his mother's lap.\r
\r
Panel.Ht.,21 1/2 inches.\r
\r
Fine Renaissance gilt carved-wood frame.\r
\r
## Pier Francesco FIORENTINO\r
\r
Florence.Painted during last quarter of 15th.century.\r
\r
The Virgin and Child, with two angels.\r
\r
The Infant Christ, golden-haired like his Mother, and all but naked, holds a bird in his left hand, its beak to his lips. The Madonna watches him, with a pensive expression of great sweetness.\r
\r
Good state of preservation.\r
\r
W.,15inches.\r
\r
Panel.Ht.,29 inches.W.,18 1/2 inches.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
## TADDEO GADDI\r
\r
Florence:died 1366\r
\r
Martyrdom of Saint Paul.\r
\r
Gold background. Numerous figures, on foot and horseback.In the foreground lies the head of the saint, crowned. The executioner is sheathing his sword. Landscape of hills and flowers, with the Cross and an angel.\r
\r
Panel.Ht.,12 inches.W.,14 inches.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
## BICCI di LORENZO\r
\r
Florence:I373-I452\r
\r
Ogival panel. St. John the Baptist, and St. Sebastian. St. John holds a long cross, and is bare-armed and bare-footed. St. Sebastian, carrying a palm-leaf and wearing a crown, is dressed in red and blue embroidered robes. The grass at their feet is full of fowers. Gold background. Fine state of preservation. In the upper part of the panel, the Angel of the Annunciation.\r
\r
Ht.,56 inches.W.,21 inches.\r
\r
From the Bardini collection,Florence.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
## BICCI di LORENZO\r
\r
Ogival panel, companion to the above. St.Antony and St. Stephen. St. Antony, aged and grey-bearded, is clad in dark colours, and carries a tau-cross and a book; a small black pig is seated at his feet. St. Stephen,in a red robe,richly embroidered, carries a stone in his right hand, symbolic of his martyrdom, and two stones are seen on either side of his tonsure. In upper part of panel, the Virgin of the Annunciation. Gold background. Fine state of preservation.\r
\r
Ht.,56 inches.W.,21 inches.\r
\r
From the Bardini collection,Florence.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
## NERI di BICCI\r
\r
Florence:I415(?)——I45I(?)\r
\r
The Virgin and Child.\r
\r
The Child clings with his left hand to the gold-embroidered white veil of his Mother. She wears a deep-red dress, richly embroidered with gold, and a dark mantle. The expression of both faces is tender and charming.\r
\r
Gold background.\r
\r
Good state ofpreservation.\r
\r
Panel.Ht.,17 inches.W.,13 1/2 inches.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
## SASSETTA (Stefano di Giovanni)\r
\r
Siena:1392-1450\r
\r
The Virgin and Child.\r
\r
The Madonna wears a black drapery over her head, and over her rose-coloured robe. The Child, dressed in a white robe embroidered with gold stars, and a rose-coloured mantle, raises his left hand in benediction.\r
\r
Gold background.\r
\r
Panel.Ht.,163/4 inches.W.,10 1/2 inches. (Illustrated.)\r
## CIMABUE\r
\r
Florence:1240 （?)—after 1302\r
\r
The Virgin.\r
\r
She is clad in a long black drapery, edged with pink and with a pink design, passing over her head; in her right hand she holds a beautifully stylised rose.The right of the Child is seen, with two fingers raised in benediction.\r
\r
Gold background.\r
\r
Part of a larger picture.\r
\r
Panel.Ht.,29 inches.W.,18 inches.\r
\r
From the Dollfus collection. (Sale in Paris,1912.)\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
## Domenico MORONE da VERONA\r
\r
Verona:1442—after1503\r
\r
Christ crucified between two thieves.\r
\r
An extremely fine and moving composition,in a setting of high cliffs crowned with cypresses. In the distance, at the end of the with clasped hands; and the Madonna faints by her side, supported by two women. Beneath the Cross, and facing it, is a soldier on ravine, is a city. By the foot of the Cross stands Mary Magdalene, horseback. In the foreground, strewn with bones, are four dogs.\r
\r
Panel. Ht.,26 inches.W.,21 inches.\r
\r
(Mr.Berenson,who assigned this attribution,ascribes to the same master a picture in the Ashmolean Museum at Oxford,representing a Dominican saint preaching before the church at Verona.)\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
## Antonio POLLAIUOLO\r
\r
Florence:1443-1496\r
\r
Portrait of a young Florentine patrician. The face is pale,beneath rich auburn hair; the dress is deep red. On the blue background, above the head,is painted a string of pearls.\r
\r
betrothal.\r
\r
This portrait was probably painted on the occasion of the sitter's\r
\r
Panel.Ht.,14 inches.W.,11 inches.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
## TINTORETTO (Jacopo Robusti)\r
\r
Venice:1518-1594\r
\r
Christ kneeling in the Garden of Olives.From the midst of a radiant cloud, an angel presents a golden chalice to the Saviour's lips. In the corner below,a bearded apostle lies sleeping.\r
\r
An important and beautiful work in the master's finest style towards the end of his career.\r
\r
Canvas. Ht.,49 inches. W., 60 1/2 inches.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
## Giovanni BELLINI\r
\r
Venice:1428-1516\r
\r
Head of the Virgin;with white hood and bright blue mantle.\r
\r
Transferred to canvas. Ht.,16 1/4 inches. W.,13 inches.\r
\r
(Attribution confirmed by Dr.Gronau.)\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
## PIETER BRUEGHEL(the EIder)\r
\r
Antwerp:1525-1569\r
\r
A rustic wedding. Signed (bottom,left)Brveghel,1544.\r
\r
From the Rudolph Kann collection;in the catalogue of which (edited by Messrs.Duveen Bros.;Paris,Igo7, Tome I,no.6) evidently owing to an error in reading the date,the picture is ascribed to Brueghel the Younger,"after Brueghel the Elder ".The picture is certainly not painted in the manner of the younger Brueghel,and was always knoen, in the Rudolph Kann collection,asa workof Brueghel the Elder:an attribution entirely corroborated byaclose reading of the date.It may be observed that the1644 reading would in any case preclude even Brueghel the younger, who died in 1638.\r
\r
Panel.Ht.,29 1/2 inches.W.,42 inches. (Illustrated.)\r
## SCHOOL of BRUGES""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

