zac:5830_lot_36 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "BOTTICINI 15th.century Adoration of the Infant Christ, who lies naked between the Virgin and St. Joseph, both kneeling, St. Joseph holding a candle. Two figures peer through a window behind them. On the left, the manger, with the ox and the ass. Glimpses of a fresh landscape of woodland, through the window, and to right and left. This fine painting has been attributed, with great likelihood, to Dirk Bouts. In perfect preservation.  Panel.Ht.,14 1/2inches.W.,11 1/2inches. (Illustrated.)" ;
