zac:5830_lot_42 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "BICCI di LORENZO  Ogival panel, companion to the above. St.Antony and St. Stephen. St. Antony, aged and grey-bearded, is clad in dark colours, and carries a tau-cross and a book; a small black pig is seated at his feet. St. Stephen,in a red robe,richly embroidered, carries a stone in his right hand, symbolic of his martyrdom, and two stones are seen on either side of his tonsure. In upper part of panel, the Virgin of the Annunciation. Gold background. Fine state of preservation.  Ht.,56 inches.W.,21 inches.  From the Bardini collection,Florence.  (Illustrated.)" ;
