zac:5830_lot_46 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "Domenico MORONE da VERONA  Verona:1442—after1503  Christ crucified between two thieves.  An extremely fine and moving composition,in a setting of high cliffs crowned with cypresses. In the distance, at the end of the with clasped hands; and the Madonna faints by her side, supported by two women. Beneath the Cross, and facing it, is a soldier on ravine, is a city. By the foot of the Cross stands Mary Magdalene, horseback. In the foreground, strewn with bones, are four dogs.  Panel. Ht.,26 inches.W.,21 inches.  (Mr.Berenson,who assigned this attribution,ascribes to the same master a picture in the Ashmolean Museum at Oxford,representing a Dominican saint preaching before the church at Verona.)  (Illustrated.)" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5830_lot_46_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5830_lot_46_id ;
