zac:5830_lot_50_title rdfs:label "PIETER BRUEGHEL(the EIder)  Antwerp:1525-1569  A rustic wedding. Signed (bottom,left)Brveghel,1544.  From the Rudolph Kann collection;in the catalogue of which (edited by Messrs.Duveen Bros.;Paris,Igo7, Tome I,no.6) evidently owing to an error in reading the date,the picture is ascribed to Brueghel the Younger,\"after Brueghel the Elder \".The picture is certainly not painted in the manner of the younger Brueghel,and was always knoen, in the Rudolph Kann collection,asa workof Brueghel the Elder:an attribution entirely corroborated byaclose reading of the date.It may be observed that the1644 reading would in any case preclude even Brueghel the younger, who died in 1638.  Panel.Ht.,29 1/2 inches.W.,42 inches. (Illustrated.)" .

zac:5830_lot_51 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "SCHOOL of BRUGES  I5th.century  Adoration of the Infant Christ, who lies naked between the Virgin and St. Joseph, both kneeling, St. Joseph holding a candle. Two figures peer through a window behind them. On the left, the manger, with the ox and the ass. Glimpses of a fresh landscape of woodland, through the window, and to right and left. This fine painting has been attributed, with great likelihood, to Dirk Bouts. In perfect preservation.  Panel.Ht.,14 1/2inches.W.,11 1/2inches. (Illustrated.)" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5830_lot_51_title ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:5830_lot_51_id ;
