zac:5830_lot_57 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "SCHOOL of AVIGNON  Early 15th.century.  The Birth of the Virgin.  St.Anne is propped up with large pillows,in a low bed with a crimson coverlet. A nurse is preparing to wash the newborn Child. On the other side of the bed,a tablewith a dish of fruit,glasses,a decanter,etc.Behind, a romanesque arcade, and a background of embossed gold.  Panel.Ht.,43 inches.W.,29 inches.  (Illustrated.) The Crucifixion.  St. John and the Virgin at the foot of the Cross,in red and blue robes. In the background, the walls of a city.  Inscribed:Benedet.Mepinta. I2I2.  Panel.Ht.,343/4inches.W.,271/4inches.  (Illustrated.)" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:5830_lot_57_title ;
